WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.740
Process what will not store, team up, and prove your results.

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:09.720
This is the video for Module 3 of Post-Harvest Management and Food Preservation.

3
00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:23.600
Some produce will not store fresh. Yams cut by the hoe, cassava that must be used within days, fish landed in the heat. Instead of watching it rot, you can turn it into a product that lasts.

4
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:33.240
Drying removes the water that moulds need. Smoking dries and coats the food. Salting draws water out and stops many germs.

5
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:41.190
Fermenting uses friendly microbes, as in garri and iru. And cooling slows breathing and germ growth.

6
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:54.430
Open sun drying on the ground lets in dust, insects, goats and rain. A solar dryer is a box or tent with a clear cover and air vents. The cover keeps all of that out.

7
00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:05.850
Wash your hands and tools, and slice on a clean board, not the floor. Cut pieces evenly so they dry at the same rate, and spread them thinly on raised trays.

8
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.270
Dry until each piece snaps cleanly. Cool, then pack at once in clean, airtight containers, labelled with the product and date.

9
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.750
Any soft piece needs more time. And any batch that shows mould must be thrown away.

10
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:34.920
When fat drips onto flames, or fish sits in thick dirty smoke, harmful compounds called PAHs build up on the fish. Improved kilns keep the fire separate and catch the fat.

11
00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:41.060
Whatever kiln you use, never burn plastic, rubber, tyres or painted wood.

12
00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:48.990
Cut yams will not store, so Funmi must decide this week. Selling them all now brings 60,000 naira.

13
00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:58.810
First she runs a small trial. 10 kg of yam gives her 2.5 kg of dry chips, a yield of 25 percent in her own hands.

14
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:17.830
So 150 kg should give about 37.5 kg of chips. At about 2,500 naira per kg, that is 93,750 naira. Her costs for firewood, labour, transport and bags are about 15,000.

15
00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:35.610
Processing leaves 78,750 naira, which is 18,750 more than selling fresh. It pays only because she measured her own yield and costs first. With no time or no buyer, selling the same day is still better.

16
00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:48.080
Some tools cost too much for one household. Extension officers from your state ADP, and NSPRI, the stored products research institute, can advise and train.

17
00:02:49.330 --> 00:03:02.840
In a group, costs shrink. One group of 15 women shared a moisture meter quoted at about 120,000 naira. That is 8,000 naira each, with written rules on who keeps it and how it is booked.

18
00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:16.310
When you ask for help, be specific. Hauwa wrote: our group of 15 measured about 7.5 percent loss, and we would like a hermetic storage demonstration before the October harvest.

19
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:26.840
Your evidence pack shows the loss point, your baseline, the change, the result measured the same way, the value minus the cost, and a 90-day plan.

20
00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:41.080
For example, Ifeoma sells garden egg near Nsukka. Her plan uses the new routine on every trip, adds a clay pot cooler, shows four other sellers her method, and updates her pack in week 13.

21
00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:52.360
Her loss fell from 12 percent to 5 percent. That is a fall of 7 percentage points, not 7 percent. Saying it correctly avoids confusion.

22
00:03:53.610 --> 00:04:06.990
Check your pack. Same storage time as the baseline, or the result looks bigger than it is. Subtract the cost. Say prices are approximate. Use several trips, not one good day. Add photos and dates.

23
00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:11.180
If something did not work, say so. Honest records build trust.

24
00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:25.630
To remember. Process food that spoils fast and has buyers, but trial it first. Keep fish away from flames. Ask partners for something specific. And measure before and after with the same method.

25
00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:35.990
Now run a small processing trial, send one specific request to a partner, and draft your evidence pack. Practise presenting it in two minutes.

26
00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.280
Continue with the lessons below.
